course: dictionary
lesson: 5718
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word loon can mean a bird, a silly person, or a boy in Scotland. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which are its context.
explain: «In Canada the one-dollar coin is called a loonie, because it has a loon on it.» A coin can show a bird, so loon here means the large water bird. Try the bird meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Rouse thee, old loon» is said to a person, not a bird. Loon here means a silly or crazy person, and the speaker is teasing them. Swap in "silly person" and see if the sentence still works.
explain: Ask yourself which meaning fits the clues. If you are not sure, a dictionary will show you every meaning, and you can pick the one that matches the sentence.
fact: A loon is a large water bird with a haunting call, and it is good at diving for fish.
fact: In the UK, the loon is called a diver.
fact: Canada's one-dollar coin is called the «loonie», because it shows a loon.
fact: «Loon» can also mean a silly, crazy or strange person, often said in a joking way.
fact: In Scotland, «loon» can mean a boy or young man.
exercise: «In Canada the one-dollar coin is called a loonie, because it has a loon on it.» What is a loon in this sentence? | *A large water bird | A boy in Scotland | A type of money | A silly person
exercise: Maya shouts, «You are a loon!» to her friend, who is juggling flaming torches. What does loon mean? | A kind of tree | A coin | *A silly, crazy person | A large water bird
exercise: «The two-dollar coin is called a toonie, and the one-dollar coin is called a loonie.» Which word is the name of the one-dollar coin? | two | dollar | *loonie | toonie
test: «He is crazy as a loon!» What does loon mean in this phrase? | A coin | A boy in Scotland | A bird that flies backwards | *A crazy person, said in a joking way
test: «The two-dollar coin is called a toonie.» What is the two-dollar coin called? | A loonie | *A toonie | A bird | A diver
exam: Ella sees a large bird dive into a lake and catch a fish, and she calls out, «Look at that loon!» Which meaning fits best? | A silly, crazy person | A coin with a picture on it | *A large water bird that dives for fish | A young man in Scotland
